### 🟡 LOW — No CORS Policy Defined

No CORS middleware is configured. Express does not restrict cross-origin requests by default in all scenarios. This can allow unauthorized domains to make credentialed requests to your API.

```javascript
const cors = require('cors');

const corsOptions = {
  origin: ['https://yourdomain.com'], // explicit allowlist — never use '*' with credentials
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  credentials: true,
  maxAge: 86400, // cache preflight for 24h
};
app.use(cors(corsOptions));
```

