### 🟡 LOW — No Structured Error Handling or Logging

Unhandled errors will crash the process or leak stack traces to clients. There is also no logging, making incident detection and forensics impossible.

```javascript
const pino = require('pino');
const logger = pino({ redact: ['req.headers.authorization', '*.password', '*.secret'] });

// Centralized error handler (must be last middleware)
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log internally with full detail
  logger.error({ err, reqId: req.id }, 'Unhandled error');

  // Respond to client with NO internal detail
  const status = err.status ?? 500;
  res.status(status).json({
    error: status < 500 ? err.message : 'An internal error occurred',
  });
});

// Catch unhandled promise rejections
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason) => {
  logger.fatal({ reason }, 'Unhandled promise rejection — shutting down');
  process.exit(1);
});
```

