### 🟡 LOW — Server Listens on All Interfaces (`0.0.0.0`)

`app.listen(3000)` binds to all network interfaces by default, including public-facing ones.

```javascript
// Bind to loopback only if behind a reverse proxy (nginx, ALB, etc.)
app.listen(3000, '127.0.0.1', () => {
  console.log('Server listening on 127.0.0.1:3000');
});
```

